WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.560
The movie so good I’ve seen it 6 times

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.560
Aquaman turns mountain man!

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.160
Michael Shannon gets paranoid

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.260
Hello, and welcome to Indie Movie Guide

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.240
I am Alicia and I cannot sing!

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.680
Yeah, I shouldn’t give up my day job

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.080
But this week in the theaters

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:28.140
I can live by curiously through Emma Stone and Ryan Gosling

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.680
and live out my fantasies of being in a musical by watching ‘La La Land’

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.660
I’m gonna tell you all about that film coming up soon

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.900
but first... let’s start off with a little psycho-sexual drama, shall we?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.880
In theaters and on video on demand this week you can catch a movie called ‘Frank &amp; Lola’

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.260
and I encourage you to seek it out

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.760
It stars Michael Shannon and Imogen Poots

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.000
and it’s all about a relationship that turns very paranoid

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.440
Clip: -You really look out for me, I’m not used to it

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.800
-Well, get used to it

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.160
-Every morning when I wake up, first thing I think of is you

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.860
-You fall in love usually Frank?

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.240
So, Frank is a talented chef, but even then he’s not quite sure he is good enough for Lola

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.200
the flighty fashion designer, and that insecurity spills out into something quite dark.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.580
Now this movie is best when it looks at the complexity of relationships

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.000
particularly from the male perspective

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.580
It does go a little bit out there with the plot

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.620
but the person that grounds it all is Michael Shannon

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.700
I cannot believe how good he is on every single film

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.700
Just think about this year alone

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.240
He’s been in ‘Midnight Special’

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.420
He was in that small but important part of ‘Loving’

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:44.220
‘Nocturnal animals’ for what he probably will get a Best Supporting Actor Nomination at the Oscars

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.140
I hope he does, and now ‘Frank &amp; Lola’

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.900
That plus the cinematography

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:54.540
and the way it looks at relationships through the psychological thriller lens

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.520
is the reason why you should try to see ‘Frank &amp; Lola’

00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.960
*Clip* -No man should be expose to that

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.080
-I love you

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:05.740
-Me too

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:13.000
Another smaller film that you should try to seek out if possible it’s called 'Sugar Mountain'

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:20.060
This is another twisted drama about two brothers who decide to fake a missing person in the mountain story

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:25.020
so they can sell that story to the media, make some money, pay off their debts

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:29.220
and also pay off this thug who is after them played by Jason Momoa

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.340
*Clip* -Caught you little runt!

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.440
-I want the money

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:34.640
-10,000 bucks

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:36.880
-We need cash

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.060
-You know… and fast

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.120
The plot of ‘Sugar Mountain’ moves at a really great pace

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.040
and the brothers get a lot more trouble that they bargain for when they go on this venture

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.040
And… Jason Momoa...

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.220
he uses his huge physique, in full force

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.040
to be this very scary thug, which is exactly what that role needed

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:00.760
-It’s a hoax

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.780
-Pardon me?

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:02.840
-A hoax

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:06.280
It’s also shot beautifully and very entertaining

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:11.220
So try to seek out ‘Sugar Mountain’ if it is playing near you this weekend

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:15.360
If it’s not, I’m sure it is gonna be on video on demand very soon.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.360
*Clip* -Hope for finding the young man alive is decreasing…

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.740
-Who has said again that there’s no evidence of foul play in the disappearance.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:26.260
Now to the film I might possibly be addicted to, because I’ve seen it 6 times

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:32.220
Actually I’m pretty sure that I am addicted to it

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.120
I’m talking about ‘La La Land’ and when you see this movie...

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.580
if you know me at all

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.760
you will understand why I love it so much

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.500
Because ‘La La Land’ is an ode to classic musicals

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.760
It’s an ode to classic movies

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.740
It’s about Los Angeles

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.840
it’s about chasing your hopes, ambitions, and dreams…

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:56.060
Also love, and the choices we make and how those choices affect you in the future

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.720
and it also stars my favorite Emma Stone

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.380
*Clip* -Maybe I’m not good enough

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.180
-Yes, you are

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:01.700
-Maybe I’m not

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:02.960
-It’s like a pipe dream

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.040
-This is the dream.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.500
It’s conflict and it’s compromise

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.340
it’s very, very exciting

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:15.240
Big awards watch on this one!

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:20.820
Possible Oscar nominations for Best Picture, for Best Lead Actress for Emma Stone

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.040
Best Lead Actor for Ryan Gosling

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.920
Best Director for Damien Chazelle

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.240
Best Production Design

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.920
Best Score, Best Song

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.260
So many more!

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.800
It’ll probably sweep most of the awards this Award season

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.340
and it definitely deserves to

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.240
It’s a bloody joy to watch

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.400
it looks beautiful, it will hit you in the feels

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.220
Everyone can relate to this

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.100
It's got great songs and dance numbers

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.100
Have I convince you yet?

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.180
If not, here is our modern day…

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.200
Ryan Gosling and Emma Stone to tell you more

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:59.400
-I love this movie so much, as someone who grew up watching classic musicals

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.760
and dreaming of moving to L.A…

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.600
I know you didn’t just make it for me, but it feels like you did.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:05.500
-You’re welcomed.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.500
It was just for you actually, that’s the secret.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.500
-This is all just for me, I appreciated.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:13.580
-After doing this film with something you have to be out of your comfort zone for

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:17.780
Do you feel more fearless in a way about movies in general?

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:22.700
-I had such an incredibly deep experience doing it

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.640
because when you put so much of yourself in something and you rehearse for so long…

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:30.200
you really give... you know, you give it your all.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:35.360
I just fell in love with that element of the process

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.200
-I would’ve thought it would be hard to look indignant while wearing yellow 80’ pants

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.020
but you pull that off pretty well.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:43.860
-Just wanted to say that

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:44.600
-Thank you

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.940
-What do you relate to with the character of Sebastian?

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.160
Or was there something in particular that you loved about him?

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.700
-I love the time in his life that you meet him in the film

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:57.360
because he’s experienced a lot of failure and rejection…

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:03.840
and he is right on the coast of becoming a very angry, bitter, person

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.220
which is the worst time to meet somebody, a potential love interest

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.080
but that’s the way it happens in the movie.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.740
-Congratulations!

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.720
-Nice jazz hands

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:33.880
So… with ‘La La Land’ now in theatres my Top 5 looks like this:

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.140
My top best movies are:

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:41.420
Moonlight, Manchester by the sea, La La Land

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.480
Arrival, Nocturnal Animals…

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:47.620
Sorry Lion, Lion still fantastic but it just goes down a step or two…

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:50.600
and so many more movies coming out towards the end of the year

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.000
so I’m sure it will change once again

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.340
I know I’m gonna get a lot of comments like:

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.900
Why you love ‘La La Land’ so much but it’s not your number one?

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:02.980
Hard to explain, but I think I look at these as the best made movies

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:05.500
and I just thought ‘Moonlight’ was something I’d never seen before

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:11.600
Here’s what I see for the top 10 contenders for the Best Picture nominees:

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:18.680
Arrival, Fences, Jackie, Hacksaw Ridge, if they’re ready to forgive Mel Gibson and they should

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:23.580
La La Land, Lion, Loving, Moonlight, Manchester by the sea

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.080
and Silence by Martin Scorsese…

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.540
Silence it’s the only one on this that I haven’t seen yet

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:33.500
but it’s getting good buzz from the few screening that it had so far.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:37.980
To recap once again what you can see this weekend:

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.760
Check out ‘La La Land’ in theatres

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.980
if it’s not playing near you right now it will be expanding in the next few weeks

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:49.840
Also in theatres and on VOD make sure you catch ‘Frank &amp; Lola’

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:52.760
and try to see ‘Sugar Mountain’ in theatres

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.940
Once again that will  probably be on video on demand later on…

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.580
so don’t fret if it’s not in your area just yet

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.640
That’s the end for another Fandango Indie Movie Guide

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:05.400
Let me know in the comments below what you think of this week’s movies

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.940
What you think of ‘La La Land’, whether I hyped this movie up way too much

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.880
I probably have, but I don’t care I’m gonna go see it for a 7th time

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.080
and I’ll see you next week. Bye!

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.540
I’m just rumbling now so, shut up Alicia!

